# Schedule Builder — LLM picks the tool, Python writes the SCHEDULE

Flow: `ScheduleBuilderAgent.open_session(agent_task)` (`app/agent.py`) binds the case packet (baseline `.INC`, includes, upstream agent data from `state.agents[*].data` — `facts`/`new_wells`, via `upstream_agent_data`; legacy `state.data.excel` fallback — HITL answers, `rework_reason`) → LLM chooses a tool → `agent.tools.run(state, name, args)` (tools in `app/agent_tools.py`, `@tool(...)` = `agent.tools.tool`) → one stored `result` per session → `GET /sessions/{id}/result` = `agent.result(state)` (builds a dirty working text first).

Layout (same as every agent service, checked by `mas-agent-kit/tests/test_service_shape.py`): `app/agent.py` — the class (`open_session`, `result`, `new_result` adds `units: METRIC`, `store_result` echoes artifact sizes, not the `.INC`) and `agent = ScheduleBuilderAgent()`; `app/agent_tools.py` — tools only; `app/main.py` — `agent_router(agent)` + deterministic domain routes (`/keywords`, `/render`, `/build`, `/apply`, `/diff`).

## Rules
- **The LLM never writes `.INC` text.** Parse/apply/emit live in `parse.py`, `timeline_ops.py`, `commissioning.py`, `group_rebind.py`, `emit.py`; keyword layout comes from `schema_catalogues.json` via `schema_renderer.py` (`render_ir`). No keyword layout hardcoded as a class per keyword.
- Tools (`@tool(...)` functions in `agent_tools.py`): `inspect_schedule`, `inspect_well`, `analyze_forecast_controls`, `search_keywords`, `get_keyword`, `render_ir`, `list_records`, `apply_commissioning`, `apply_group_rebind(spec)`, `apply_operations`, `build_schedule`, `validate_result`, `ask_engineer`. Adding one = a function here (`agent.store_result(state, agent.new_result(...))` for result tools) + `TOOLS` row in the generator (`tool_http`) + `SYSTEM` «когда вызывать» + smoke + pytest.
- Incomplete spec → `_spec_incomplete(...)` for the LLM (where to find the data: task, GRUPTREE, baseline, `engineer_answers`). A human is asked only via `ask_engineer` (prose, `human_text_problems`, options from baseline/GRUPTREE — never `GNEW/GINJ/GPROD` placeholders).
- One result per session: after `apply_*`/`ask_engineer` stored a result, further result-producing calls return `result_already_stored` — the LLM must stop, not re-word.
- New-well facts priority in `_new_well_defs`: engineer HITL answer (`new_wells_policy` table) → `new_wells` from the agent that read Excel (`state.agents[*].data.new_wells`, `extract_well_parameters`) → `inputs.new_wells` **only if dict rows** (bare well names from the Decision LLM are not definitions).
- Unlisted-wells policy (`keep|remove`) comes from the HITL `choice`, never regex on the label; `remove` touches only named wells (`_is_named_well`), never `*`/`?` wildcards (`WEFAC '*'`).
- Summaries are counts and well lists: «Сдвинул даты ввода 4 скважин: 1601 → 1 FEB 2020 …», «Добавил 10 скважин — WELSPECS, COMPDATMD и WCONPROD», «Убрал из прогноза …».
- Emit invariants (also `.cursor/rules/schedule-syntax-self-apply-smoke.mdc`): every table keyword ends with a bare `/` plus a blank line; keyword order per `schedule_emit_order.py`; INCLUDE safety untouched.

